On the JSON side, I've seen parsing eat a surprising chunk of runtime in ingest-heavy jobs. Streaming beats loading everything at once, and it's worth benchmarking the parser itself, since stdlib json isn't always the bottleneck. Also watch serialization round-trips: converting between formats repeatedly adds up fast.

